1
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:49,960
Come on, Bro.

2
00:00:53,085 --> 00:00:56,001
Whoo! Whoo, whoo, whoo!

3
00:01:05,126 --> 00:01:06,751
Whoo!

4
00:01:10,835 --> 00:01:12,125
Whoo!

5
00:01:12,126 --> 00:01:13,959
Whoa. Whoa.

6
00:01:13,960 --> 00:01:15,042
Hey, watch it.

7
00:01:15,043 --> 00:01:16,875
You were in my way, Bro.

8
00:01:16,876 --> 00:01:18,376
Oh, okay.

9
00:01:19,043 --> 00:01:21,168
Whoo--

10
00:01:24,418 --> 00:01:25,626
Whoo!

11
00:01:29,626 --> 00:01:30,835
Whoo!

12
00:01:32,501 --> 00:01:34,084
Whoo!

13
00:01:34,085 --> 00:01:35,542
Is that
all you got?

14
00:01:35,543 --> 00:01:37,668
You want to go faster, huh?

15
00:01:45,626 --> 00:01:47,710
Whoo-hoo!

16
00:01:54,168 --> 00:01:55,501
That was cool, Bro.

17
00:01:56,168 --> 00:01:57,751
<i>Skxawng</i>, let go.

18
00:02:01,043 --> 00:02:02,375
It was cool riding
with you, Bro.

19
00:02:02,376 --> 00:02:03,668
High four.

20
00:02:12,001 --> 00:02:13,668
All right,
I got to get back, Bro.

21
00:02:14,501 --> 00:02:15,751
Little Brother,

22
00:02:16,376 --> 00:02:18,376
tell me one thing
before you go.

23
00:02:21,001 --> 00:02:22,210
How did I die?

24
00:02:28,876 --> 00:02:30,335
You got shot.

25
00:02:31,876 --> 00:02:34,043
We could have escaped, but I
made us go back for Spider.

26
00:02:35,251 --> 00:02:36,585
Then we had to go back.

27
00:02:37,376 --> 00:02:38,459
That's not your fault.

28
00:02:38,460 --> 00:02:39,626
Tell that to Dad.

29
00:02:40,210 --> 00:02:42,293
We weren't even supposed
to be out there.

30
00:02:43,710 --> 00:02:46,625
I got us caught
because I disobeyed orders.

31
00:02:46,626 --> 00:02:48,418
That's just you, Little Bro.

32
00:02:58,835 --> 00:03:00,210
I love you, Brother.

33
00:03:00,835 --> 00:03:01,835
<i>Skxawng.</i>

34
00:03:07,751 --> 00:03:09,335
<i>I killed my brother.</i>

35
00:03:10,210 --> 00:03:11,418
<i>No matter what happens,</i>

36
00:03:12,168 --> 00:03:15,543
<i>I have to live with that
for the rest of my life.</i>

37
00:03:54,043 --> 00:03:55,126
I wish I could do it.

38
00:03:55,668 --> 00:03:57,710
No, I wish I could do it.

39
00:03:59,460 --> 00:04:02,084
If I have another
stupid seizure underwater...

40
00:04:02,085 --> 00:04:03,167
Yeah,

41
00:04:03,168 --> 00:04:05,000
you'd be me
without a mask.

42
00:04:07,335 --> 00:04:08,750
- Uh, let's test that.
- Hey, hey.

43
00:04:08,751 --> 00:04:10,292
- Watch it.
- See what happens.

44
00:04:10,293 --> 00:04:11,418
Hey, watch the stitches.

45
00:04:12,543 --> 00:04:14,417
Uh-huh. Yeah,
how do you like that, huh?

46
00:04:14,418 --> 00:04:15,418
No! Ow!

47
00:04:38,293 --> 00:04:39,959
<i>The fire of hate</i>

48
00:04:39,960 --> 00:04:41,835
<i>leaves only
the ash of grief.</i>

49
00:04:43,793 --> 00:04:45,209
<i>My mother mourned</i>

50
00:04:45,210 --> 00:04:46,293
<i>the ancient way,</i>

51
00:04:46,835 --> 00:04:49,376
<i>singing her son's life
during the daily eclipse.</i>

52
00:04:51,293 --> 00:04:53,168
<i>Because the light
always returns.</i>

53
00:05:02,710 --> 00:05:03,835
<i>There's the</i> Na'vi <i>way,</i>

54
00:05:04,835 --> 00:05:06,335
<i>and then there's
my dad's way.</i>

55
00:05:07,043 --> 00:05:09,418
<i>Say nothing.
Keep busy.</i>

56
00:05:28,251 --> 00:05:30,501
<i>The Reef People say
the sea washes you clean.</i>

57
00:05:32,001 --> 00:05:33,584
<i>Washes away your sins.</i>

58
00:06:10,543 --> 00:06:11,543
What do you got?

59
00:06:13,376 --> 00:06:14,792
You're supposed
to be collecting guns.

60
00:06:14,793 --> 00:06:16,251
That thing's useless.

61
00:06:16,835 --> 00:06:17,960
Focus, boy.

62
00:06:23,710 --> 00:06:25,335
Don't let your mother
see that.

63
00:06:34,376 --> 00:06:35,375
Hey, excuse me.

64
00:06:35,376 --> 00:06:36,917
- Sorry.
- Excuse me.

65
00:06:36,918 --> 00:06:38,043
- Tuk.
- Sorry.

66
00:06:45,126 --> 00:06:46,126
Bro.

67
00:06:47,751 --> 00:06:49,001
Ah, sick.

68
00:06:50,418 --> 00:06:51,418
What is this?

69
00:06:52,668 --> 00:06:53,668
Tsireya?

70
00:06:55,168 --> 00:06:56,501
What are you doing?

71
00:06:58,876 --> 00:07:01,417
This is an AR, all right?

72
00:07:01,418 --> 00:07:03,542
This is the mag.
It's where the bullets are.

73
00:07:03,543 --> 00:07:04,710
Empty.

74
00:07:05,626 --> 00:07:06,626
Slap it.

75
00:07:07,585 --> 00:07:08,625
Rack it.

76
00:07:08,626 --> 00:07:10,000
And then, boom,

77
00:07:10,001 --> 00:07:11,125
you can just spray.

78
00:07:11,126 --> 00:07:13,375
You can kill
a lot of Sky People with this.

79
00:07:13,376 --> 00:07:15,542
See? Ceramic action.

80
00:07:15,543 --> 00:07:17,667
You clean 'em and oil 'em,
be as good as new.

81
00:07:17,668 --> 00:07:19,750
This is not the <i>Na'vi</i> way,

82
00:07:19,751 --> 00:07:20,959
<i>Jakesully</i>.

83
00:07:20,960 --> 00:07:23,125
Weapons of metal
are forbidden.

84
00:07:23,126 --> 00:07:24,209
You know this.

85
00:07:24,210 --> 00:07:25,292
To touch them

86
00:07:25,293 --> 00:07:26,710
poisons the heart.

87
00:07:27,210 --> 00:07:28,292
Eywa

88
00:07:28,293 --> 00:07:29,376
will provide.

89
00:07:30,001 --> 00:07:31,876
Right.

90
00:07:32,918 --> 00:07:35,292
The mourning period
is not even over.

91
00:07:35,293 --> 00:07:36,209
Tuk.

92
00:07:36,210 --> 00:07:37,667
You should be
with your family,

93
00:07:37,668 --> 00:07:39,459
not gathering these things.

94
00:07:39,460 --> 00:07:41,042
Your woman

95
00:07:41,043 --> 00:07:42,168
needs you.

96
00:07:44,210 --> 00:07:47,210
My son lies with the ancestors
in the reef.

97
00:07:48,085 --> 00:07:49,709
This is our home.

98
00:07:49,710 --> 00:07:51,667
I said I would stand and fight,

99
00:07:51,668 --> 00:07:54,459
but I can't fight gunships
with spears.

100
00:07:54,460 --> 00:07:56,375
We sank the demon ship.

101
00:07:56,376 --> 00:07:58,126
The pink skins fear us now.

102
00:07:59,751 --> 00:08:01,792
Yeah? We got lucky.

103
00:08:01,793 --> 00:08:03,251
And they got many more ships.

104
00:08:04,043 --> 00:08:05,460
Least we got these.

105
00:08:06,668 --> 00:08:09,001
We are grateful you
stand with us, <i>Jakesully</i>.

106
00:08:09,668 --> 00:08:11,084
It is not guns we need.

107
00:08:11,085 --> 00:08:12,501
It is Rider of Last Shadow.

108
00:08:14,293 --> 00:08:16,000
Ride great <i>toruk</i>

109
00:08:16,001 --> 00:08:18,043
as you did before.

110
00:08:18,710 --> 00:08:22,709
When you ride the beast,

111
00:08:22,710 --> 00:08:24,043
you become the beast.

112
00:08:25,335 --> 00:08:27,418
And the more blood,
the better.

113
00:08:29,085 --> 00:08:31,042
I will not become

114
00:08:31,043 --> 00:08:33,001
<i>Toruk Makto</i> again.

115
00:08:34,043 --> 00:08:35,251
<i>Jakesully</i>,

116
00:08:36,210 --> 00:08:38,335
you are always <i>Toruk Makto.</i>

117
00:08:39,501 --> 00:08:41,543
Come. Rotxo.

118
00:08:47,210 --> 00:08:48,251
<i>Can you hear me?</i>

119
00:08:48,876 --> 00:08:50,167
Yeah, we can
hear you loud and clear.

120
00:08:50,168 --> 00:08:51,168
Go on, Doc.

121
00:08:52,085 --> 00:08:55,417
<i>So, uh, we've been through
the wreck, inside and out.</i>

122
00:08:55,418 --> 00:08:58,585
<i>Uh, we've searched to about
a 200-meter radius around it.</i>

123
00:08:59,126 --> 00:09:00,709
<i>We didn't find
any</i> Na'vi <i>bodies.</i>

124
00:09:00,710 --> 00:09:03,792
<i>Just crew or...
what's left of 'em.</i>

125
00:09:03,793 --> 00:09:06,167
Well, keep looking, Doctor.

126
00:09:06,168 --> 00:09:08,459
- Expand the search radius.
- <i>Roger that.</i>

127
00:09:08,460 --> 00:09:09,375
<i>Of note though,</i>

128
00:09:09,376 --> 00:09:11,376
<i>I did find an interesting
new algae.</i>

129
00:09:13,168 --> 00:09:14,667
<i>Hello? Can you hear me?</i>

130
00:09:14,668 --> 00:09:16,959
- Sully is still out there.
- We don't know that.

131
00:09:16,960 --> 00:09:19,125
Scavengers could have
carried off the bodies.

132
00:09:19,126 --> 00:09:21,667
Nope. He made it out.

133
00:09:21,668 --> 00:09:25,167
And he's in this area.
Down to a handful of villages.

134
00:09:25,168 --> 00:09:26,709
You just give me a ship
and I'll--

135
00:09:26,710 --> 00:09:27,875
I gave you a ship.

136
00:09:27,876 --> 00:09:29,626
It's right there,
on the bottom.

137
00:09:30,376 --> 00:09:31,793
Yeah. Along with my crew.

138
00:09:32,626 --> 00:09:33,626
All dead.

139
00:09:34,626 --> 00:09:36,459
You brought me out here,

140
00:09:36,460 --> 00:09:38,584
twenty-six trillion miles,

141
00:09:38,585 --> 00:09:40,292
for a single mission,

142
00:09:40,293 --> 00:09:41,875
a kinetic hard kill op

143
00:09:41,876 --> 00:09:43,876
against one guy.

144
00:09:44,418 --> 00:09:46,335
I ain't backing off.

145
00:09:50,001 --> 00:09:52,085
<i>Are we still connected? Hello?</i>

146
00:09:53,210 --> 00:09:54,793
<i>Do they have me on mute?</i>

147
00:10:01,710 --> 00:10:04,085
The spirit of my ancestors
is in this bow.

148
00:10:06,543 --> 00:10:07,751
It was our strength.

149
00:10:10,918 --> 00:10:13,376
I can help you
fix it, Lo'ak.

150
00:10:15,085 --> 00:10:16,085
No!

151
00:10:17,335 --> 00:10:18,418
It's ruined!

152
00:10:19,626 --> 00:10:21,626
<i>Everything I touch
gets ruined.</i>

153
00:10:26,751 --> 00:10:28,251
<i>They never talked about it.</i>

154
00:10:30,293 --> 00:10:31,751
<i>But it was there
in the room.</i>

155
00:10:32,376 --> 00:10:34,334
<i>Like a crouching thanator.</i>

156
00:10:37,501 --> 00:10:39,626
I know you will never
give up your bow.

157
00:10:41,626 --> 00:10:42,626
So...

158
00:10:47,501 --> 00:10:49,251
Just don't be close
when it hits.

159
00:11:08,043 --> 00:11:10,210
So, you agree with Ronal?

160
00:11:14,001 --> 00:11:15,959
I will never speak against
my husband

161
00:11:15,960 --> 00:11:17,460
in front of that woman.

162
00:11:20,085 --> 00:11:21,293
Look, I'm a marine.

163
00:11:23,251 --> 00:11:25,126
I'm not taking a knife
to a gunfight.

164
00:11:27,335 --> 00:11:28,460
Or a prayer.

165
00:11:31,126 --> 00:11:32,835
So, what am I
supposed to do?

166
00:11:33,918 --> 00:11:36,376
I can't run.
I can't fight.

167
00:11:36,876 --> 00:11:37,876
Oh, that's right.

168
00:11:38,543 --> 00:11:41,625
Eywa will provide. Yeah?
So, where was Eywa?

169
00:11:41,626 --> 00:11:43,417
Where was Eywa
when our son--

170
00:11:43,418 --> 00:11:44,418
Jake!

171
00:11:47,085 --> 00:11:49,626
I'm in this place
where I have nothing.

172
00:11:50,835 --> 00:11:53,460
Not my people,
not my forest.

173
00:11:54,918 --> 00:11:56,835
Even my father's bow
is gone.

174
00:11:59,835 --> 00:12:00,960
All I have...

175
00:12:02,251 --> 00:12:03,501
is my faith

176
00:12:04,335 --> 00:12:06,751
that this is
the Great Mother's plan.

177
00:12:09,710 --> 00:12:11,293
You have this family.

178
00:12:25,501 --> 00:12:26,835
And you have me.

179
00:12:29,126 --> 00:12:31,085
And I love you so much.

180
00:12:54,585 --> 00:12:56,709
Yeah, Payakan,
you're the man!

181
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:24,960
Whoa. Bro, Bro.

182
00:13:28,210 --> 00:13:30,710
This is sick!

183
00:13:32,960 --> 00:13:35,001
- Whoo! Whoo!
- Whoo-hoo!

184
00:13:37,001 --> 00:13:38,501
Whoo!

185
00:13:45,293 --> 00:13:47,043
- Whoo!
- Bro, come on! Go, go, go, go!

186
00:13:47,751 --> 00:13:49,543
- Oh, sh...
- Yeah!

187
00:13:54,668 --> 00:13:56,334
That was insane, cuz.

188
00:13:56,335 --> 00:13:57,501
I know, right, Bro?

189
00:13:59,668 --> 00:14:00,835
I thought you were dead.

190
00:14:04,751 --> 00:14:07,500
It sucks that Payakan
is still an outcast.

191
00:14:07,501 --> 00:14:09,375
Yeah. After saving
all our asses.

192
00:14:09,376 --> 00:14:11,084
No.
I'm sorry,

193
00:14:11,085 --> 00:14:13,167
but by the <i>tulkun</i> way,
he bears the deaths.

194
00:14:14,168 --> 00:14:15,585
All those
who died in the battle.

195
00:14:16,501 --> 00:14:17,876
He bears those deaths.

196
00:14:20,043 --> 00:14:22,835
I'm sorry. You saved us all.

197
00:14:29,501 --> 00:14:31,334
Forever, Brother.

198
00:14:31,335 --> 00:14:32,417
Always.

199
00:14:45,376 --> 00:14:46,376
Dad!

200
00:14:50,585 --> 00:14:52,334
- Wait, where's the spare?
- It's in the basket, I think.

201
00:14:52,335 --> 00:14:53,667
Hey! Wake up! Where is it?

202
00:14:53,668 --> 00:14:55,542
- Hey! Where's the spare mask?
- What?

203
00:14:55,543 --> 00:14:57,292
Where's the spare mask?
Used to be there. Where is it?

204
00:14:57,293 --> 00:14:58,709
- I don't know.
- Find it.

205
00:14:58,710 --> 00:15:00,542
- It's not here.
- Speak to me. Where is it?

206
00:15:00,543 --> 00:15:02,625
- I can't find it.
- Hey, hey! Where is it?

207
00:15:02,626 --> 00:15:04,043
- Come on. Come on. Come on.
- I got it. Dad.

208
00:15:04,585 --> 00:15:06,210
- Dad. I found it.
- Hurry.

209
00:15:11,418 --> 00:15:13,209
Spider, no.

210
00:15:13,210 --> 00:15:14,292
Breathe.

211
00:15:14,293 --> 00:15:16,292
- Breathe.
- Breathe.

212
00:15:16,293 --> 00:15:17,668
Deep and slow.

213
00:15:18,335 --> 00:15:19,501
Deep and slow.

214
00:15:20,001 --> 00:15:21,417
There you go.
You're okay.

215
00:15:21,418 --> 00:15:24,543
I'm good.
I'm good. I'm okay.

216
00:15:26,710 --> 00:15:28,835
<i>Skxawng.</i>
You have to be careful.

217
00:15:29,376 --> 00:15:31,000
- Careful's my middle name.
- Yeah, <i>skxawng.</i>

218
00:15:31,001 --> 00:15:32,542
You should be more careful,
little baby.

219
00:15:32,543 --> 00:15:33,625
Pay attention.

220
00:15:33,626 --> 00:15:36,417
- Get off. Get off. Get off.
- Stupid is your middle name.

221
00:15:36,418 --> 00:15:37,500
- Be careful, little baby.
- No, let him go.

222
00:15:37,501 --> 00:15:39,584
- You have to pay attention.
<i>- Skxawng</i> is his middle name.

223
00:15:39,585 --> 00:15:41,834
- Are you sure you're okay?
- Yeah, I feel fine.

224
00:15:44,001 --> 00:15:45,125
The Windtraders.

225
00:15:45,126 --> 00:15:46,918
The Windtraders are here.

226
00:15:48,543 --> 00:15:49,750
The Windtraders
are coming.

227
00:15:49,751 --> 00:15:50,834
Come on!

228
00:15:50,835 --> 00:15:51,960
Come on. Let's go.

229
00:15:52,460 --> 00:15:53,668
Come on.

230
00:15:54,626 --> 00:15:55,750
Come on, Tuk.

231
00:15:59,543 --> 00:16:01,168
Whoo!

232
00:16:18,085 --> 00:16:20,376
Hey!

233
00:16:35,710 --> 00:16:36,710
Tsireya.

234
00:16:40,376 --> 00:16:42,084
Look.

235
00:16:42,085 --> 00:16:43,709
Look at him.

236
00:16:43,710 --> 00:16:45,293
He's not going
to take up much room.

237
00:16:46,001 --> 00:16:47,501
As long as he's no trouble.

238
00:16:48,501 --> 00:16:50,375
- Take a knee. Let's go. Tuk.
- Kiri.

239
00:16:50,376 --> 00:16:51,834
- Come on, Kiri.
- What?

240
00:16:51,835 --> 00:16:53,709
- Kiri, please.
- Children, please sit down.

241
00:16:53,710 --> 00:16:54,751
Please, sit.

242
00:16:56,251 --> 00:16:59,001
Your mother and I have
come to a decision.

243
00:17:04,085 --> 00:17:06,084
Spider, you're going to live
back in High Camp with Norm.

244
00:17:06,085 --> 00:17:07,834
- What?
- The Windtraders will take you.

245
00:17:07,835 --> 00:17:09,875
- No, Dad.
- No, Dad. He can't.

246
00:17:09,876 --> 00:17:12,375
Spider, you can't live
in a mask

247
00:17:12,376 --> 00:17:13,459
day and night.

248
00:17:13,460 --> 00:17:15,375
I just want
to stay here with you.

249
00:17:15,376 --> 00:17:18,085
- I know, but it's too risky.
- This isn't fair.

250
00:17:18,918 --> 00:17:21,084
Please. You're the only family
I've ever known.

251
00:17:21,085 --> 00:17:22,584
This is what's
best for you.

252
00:17:22,585 --> 00:17:24,334
But, Dad,
he's our best friend.

253
00:17:24,335 --> 00:17:25,709
Can't we just
find a way?

254
00:17:25,710 --> 00:17:26,792
It's too dangerous.

255
00:17:26,793 --> 00:17:29,125
You're one dead battery away
from being dead yourself.

256
00:17:29,126 --> 00:17:31,292
He belongs
with his own kind.

257
00:17:31,293 --> 00:17:32,126
Mom.

258
00:17:32,751 --> 00:17:35,834
And what kind
is that, Mother? Alien?

259
00:17:35,835 --> 00:17:37,209
- Kiri.
- Pink-ass.

260
00:17:37,210 --> 00:17:38,292
- Kiri.
- Stop.

261
00:17:38,293 --> 00:17:40,751
You hate them so much,
